    short: "The visibility of Frallation creates a space where its image can be taken and worn by choice.",
    full: `Performed Frallation Marks
The visibility of Frallation creates a space where its image can be taken and worn by choice. Some seek to carry the appearance of the condition through deliberate marking of the skin. Thick, branching tattoos follow anatomical lines, echoing the root structures. These designs often carry a clarity and symmetry that reflect intention. They hold a fixed shape, chosen and completed in a single act.
Others pursue the finer layer. Thin markings are drawn across the body in fragmented forms that resemble script. These designs aim for irregularity, layering shapes that suggest movement and continuation. They seek to capture the feeling of something forming rather than something finished. The result carries a tension between intention and imitation, where the marks hold stillness instead of growth.
Motivations gather around identity and meaning. Some wear these markings as a way to embody intensity, to align themselves with something that feels deeper than ordinary presence. Some feel a closeness to the condition within their own thoughts and give it form upon the skin. Some believe the marks reveal something already present within them, and the act of marking becomes a form of acknowledgement.
Those who carry true Frallation recognise the difference through proximity. The marks of the condition hold variation that continues to unfold. The surface shifts subtly over time, gathering density in some places and thinning in others. The performed marks remain as they were made. This distinction settles quietly within shared spaces, shaping perception without needing to be spoken.`,
