    full: `Vanta Points
People leave little pieces of themselves behind.
The Diviners gave those fragments a name. Vanta Points, usually shortened to VP, measure the Vanta that gathers within a person as desire presses against the walls of the soul. Every hope held too tightly, every fear left unresolved, every promise carried a little longer than comfort allows leaves another trace. Most people shed those traces without ever noticing. The world quietly collects them.
Soulless produce VP more readily than Soulful people. Their hearts hold desire differently, drawing Vanta inward instead of letting it flow naturally through the soul. The same pressure that hastens Frallation also fills their pockets. What burdens one life becomes another person's livelihood.
That strange exchange gave birth to an entire economy.
Merchants buy and sell with VP alongside ordinary currency. Diviners measure it. Researchers chart it. Shard vendors welcome it with quiet smiles. Somewhere along the way, people accepted that longing could have purchasing power.
The relationship between VP and Soul Resonance reaches deeper than commerce.
As a person's resonance strengthens through hardship, conviction, understanding, and the will to continue, their soul stirs more powerfully against the Vanta gathered within. Growth leaves echoes. Every victory over despair, every monster overcome, every impossible choice survived strengthens that resonance, drawing more VP into existence. The soul reaches further, and the world answers.
Many practitioners spend VP to strengthen themselves. The process feels strangely intuitive, as though accumulated desire settles into the soul and reshapes it from within. Greater resilience. Sharper instincts. Stronger Affinities. People describe the sensation differently, yet they all speak of becoming a little more themselves afterward.
VP does not remain fixed forever, though. Desire seeks movement, and conviction gives it shape. When a person suffers defeat, yields to despair, or watches their purpose collapse beneath them, that shape begins to loosen. The Vanta gathered within scatters back into the world, carried away through the soul's weakening resonance. Most people experience this as a lingering emptiness after failure, a quiet sense that something inside them has slipped away. Diviners simply learned how to measure it.
This is why defeat carries an unseen cost. A battle lost, an ambition abandoned, or a spirit broken all release fragments of accumulated VP. The body may survive, yet the will stumbles, and the world quietly reclaims what certainty once held together.
Perhaps that is why people speak of courage as something that must be found again. They are gathering more than confidence. They are gathering themselves.
I still find that curious. A world where courage becomes currency. Where perseverance can be counted. Where the weight inside someone's heart can be exchanged for bread, medicine, or a polished shard sitting quietly on a merchant's shelf.
Perhaps value always began there. People simply learned how to mint it.
Though, I do like the saying:
Every Vanta Point is a fragment of desire suspended between Psyn and Vu~etsu, between the human soul and the ideals it strives toward.`,
